From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:12:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06903/11362] [outer-loop] ls20: L5 SOLVED round 7 (codex,
 targeted fix worked)

Round-7 gpt-5.6-sol session executed the exact targeted hypothesis
queued from round 6's near-miss: finance color 8 via the newly-found
top-middle ring instead of the upper-left ring, closing the
one-action gap that blocked every prior attempt. Key precision: the
top-middle ring can be entered on the EXACT action that decrements the
counter from 2 to 0, resetting it to 42 before the next-action-death
rule fires -- a timing window not previously exploited.

Full winning sequence: 303 actions (244-action banked prefix + a
59-action L5 tail). The source agent's own reproduction_verified is
honestly false (budget ran out before a fresh-reset gate could be
re-run), but the outer loop independently verified regardless: 5x
fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver priority branch, all 5
confirmed level=5, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: ls20 levels_reproduced 4 -> 5.
reproducible_total_levels 160 -> 161 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
